,"user":{"login":"morganholly","id":98441016,"node_id":"U_kgDOBd4XOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98441016?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly","html_url":"https://github.com/morganholly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morganholly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T09:16:11Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T09:16:11Z","body":"happens for me as well. it was fine and then started happening while editing a shader and then would happen on a different mesh with a default material.\n\nit does not show up when in the motion vector debug mode, and does show up in display lighting.\n\nif i add a new box mesh in the same scene, it shows on all faces. if i create a new box mesh in a new scene, it only shows on the bottom. if i paste the existing box mesh in, same thing. if i paste in the existing box mesh and the environment, it shows on all faces. very confusing.\n\nmac intel radeon pro 560x sonoma","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3455375092/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3771929986","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110732#issuecomment-3771929986","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110732","id":3771929986,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g0xWC","user":{"login":"jeffreytheobald","id":6026051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjYwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6026051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald","html_url":"https://github.com/jeffreytheobald","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T09:41:07Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T16:19:14Z","body":"I hope I'm not adding confusion but I found it happens with almost all models, and doesn't even require a blender model import.  It is enough just to create CSGSphere in 4.5 or later (strangely enough 3dMesh with Sphere does not seem to cause it, might be hidden by a higher poly count).  Even switching to mobile renderer (and restarting) does not solve the issue.  \n\nVideo below shows the problem:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ypCOBQMFvL4\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n* Create a 3d Scene\n* Create a new CSGSphere3D (or import a blender model)\n* Create a new standard material for it and set the colour to dark (even this isn't really necessary, just makes it easier to see)\n\nMachine:\n* Macbook Pro 16\" (2019) \n* Intel Mac Pro Intel Core i7\n* AMD Radeon Pro 5300M 4 GB\n\nGodot Version:\n* occurs on v4.5.0 and 4.5.1\n* does not occur on 4.4.1","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3771929986/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3773437160","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110732#issuecomment-3773437160","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110732","id":3773437160,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g6hTo","user":{"login":"resistdesign","id":356375,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjM3NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/356375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign","html_url":"https://github.com/resistdesign","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T15:24:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T15:24:24Z","body":"@jeffreytheobald Does it give warnings about not being able to calculate tangents?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3773437160/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3773734875","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110732#issuecomment-3773734875","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110732","id":3773734875,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g7p_b","user":{"login":"jeffreytheobald","id":6026051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjYwNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6026051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald","html_url":"https://github.com/jeffreytheobald","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffreytheobald/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T16:11:29Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T16:38:23Z","body":"No, no warnings, no errors. No output of any significance, just the editor operations.  But I might not be getting all the logs you're getting. And just to clarify, the reason I found this is it was hitting all my blender models as well, looking more carefully I can see it only happens with metallic surfaces:\n\n<img width=\"1904\" height=\"1207\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e3d58cc-75c3-4c36-83d9-b8491a20d3fa\" />\n\nI just confirmed that shifting to the mobile renderer does fix for the blender model case, but it _doesn't_ for the CSGSphere (at least in the editor).  @resistdesign what happens with CSGSphere on your setup?\n\nThe other weird thing about this bug is how incredibly consistent it is: it doesn't look glitchy.  If it was floating point errors, I'd expect it to sort of disappear at certain angles, or be a bit jaggy, but the wireframes are consistently visible from most angles, even on a totally flat metallic surface.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3773734875/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3774870963","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110732#issuecomment-3774870963","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110732","id":3774870963,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g__Wz","user":{"login":"resistdesign","id":356375,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjM3NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/356375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign","html_url":"https://github.com/resistdesign","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/resistdesign/events{/privacy}","receive